# Workshop vs GitHub copy

Single repo. **Maintain `src/<Mod>/README.md` only.** Then `npm run desc`. Do not hand-edit `Description.txt`. Reverse: `npm run readme`.

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/<Mod>/README.md` | source + GitHub (Markdown) |
| `src/<Mod>/Description.txt` | generated Workshop paste (BBCode) |
| root `README.md` | Collection, generated mods table, commands, MIT |
| `package.json` `oniMods` | steamId / workshopTitle |

## README.md

English first, `---`, Chinese. Compat_All.png in both languages. Steam Workshop line after the first image (`npm run desc` strips it). **Recommended** / **建议订阅** = optional; say the mod runs alone. Do not mark Workshop Required items unless load fails without them. Adding a mod: `oniMods` stub + `src/<Mod>/README.md`; `npm run desc` rebuilds the root table. After publish, `npm run steam-ids`.

`[MPM]` inside `[url]…[/url]` or Markdown `[text](url)` breaks. Write `(MPM)`.

## Description.txt

Generated BBCode. Steam does not render `[table]`, `[color]`, `[size]`, `[spoiler]`, `[previewyoutube]`.

## Steam IDs

`npm run steam-ids` scrapes `steamcommunity.com/id/<steam.vanity>/myworkshopfiles/?appid=457140`. Match `workshopTitle`, `mod.yaml` title, or spaced PascalCase. No Web API key. This PC: Watt Toolkit empties Node `fetch`; `scripts/steam-ids.mjs` uses `curl.exe -k`. Skip `browsefilter=mysubmissions`.
